    "title": "Arkansas Defeats Mississippi in College Basketball Game",
    "text": "• Arkansas defeated Mississippi with a score of 94-87 on Wednesday night.\n• The game took place in Oxford, Mississippi.\n• Darius Acuff, Jr. scored 26 points and had nine assists for Arkansas.\n• Five Arkansas players scored in double figures.\n• Arkansas is ranked No. 15.\n• Arkansas' record is 12-3 overall and 2-0 in the SEC.\n• Arkansas went on a 14-6 run in the second half to take a 76-61 lead.\n• The win ended Arkansas' three-game losing streak to Ole Miss.\n• Arkansas shot 22 of 30 (73%) from the free throw line.\n• Trevon Brazile scored 18 points for Arkansas.\n• Billy Richmond III and Meleek Thomas each scored 13 points for Arkansas.\n• Karter Knox scored 10 points for Arkansas.\n• Ilias Kamardine and Malik Dia each scored 16 points for Ole Miss.\n• AJ Storr scored 12 points for Ole Miss.\n• Eduardo Klafke scored 11 points for Ole Miss.\n• Patton Pinkins scored 10 points for Ole Miss.\n• Arkansas had a 10-2 run in the final two minutes of the first half.\n• Arkansas led 42-32 at halftime.\n• Arkansas will play Auburn on Saturday.\n• Ole Miss will host Missouri on Saturday.",
